From 94c8655d2f5938d62ec0159ef69c25de08983740 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:41:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plugins): evict plugin modules from a sys.modules
 snapshot; a concurrent import no longer drops a random plugin [daveey]

Problem: hermes-hub agent.log logged "Failed to load plugin '<x>': dictionary
changed size during iteration" every 10-40 min, a different plugin each time
(session-outcome, krea, deepinfra, openai, nous, telegram-platform,
browser-browserbase, meta-ai-image-gen; 2026-10-29/30). That process then ran
without the plugin (for session-outcome: no judge, gate or tool).

Why 1: _load_directory_module raised RuntimeError before exec_module, so
  _load_plugin's except recorded loaded.error and skipped register() -
  evidence: every failing plugin is a directory plugin; the new end-to-end
  test reproduces loaded.error == "dictionary changed size during iteration".
Why 2: _evict_modules (plugins_loader.py:157) built its list with
  `for n in sys.modules`, walking the live dict - evidence: a 5 s stress
  (thread churning sys.modules while calling _evict_modules) raised 24 times.
Why 3: the gateway imports on other threads at any time (agent turns, cron,
  kanban, other plugins' deadline-worker threads), and per-module import locks
  do not serialize sys.modules writes against a Python-level iteration.
Root (happened): module eviction assumed exclusive access to a process-global
  dict; the same pattern was copied into plugin_host_child (unload and failed
  import), _launchers and plugin_dev.
Root (not caught): the failure was logged as a WARNING with no traceback
  (exc_info only under HERMES_PLUGINS_DEBUG), so the message never pointed at
  Hermes code, and no test loaded a plugin while another thread imported.
Recurrence: first fix for this race.

Countermeasures:
- symptom/root: every sys.modules scan in the plugin paths iterates
  sys.modules.copy() (one C call, atomic under the GIL); plugin_host_child gets
  a shared _evict_modules helper.
- detection: "Failed to load plugin" warnings now end with
  "(raised at <file>:<line> in <func>)" for the innermost frame.
- tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_plugins_loader.py): a trap key makes a second
  thread insert into sys.modules mid-scan, deterministically.
  test_evict_modules_tolerates_concurrent_import,
  test_plugin_host_child_evict_tolerates_concurrent_import and
  test_directory_plugin_loads_while_another_thread_imports fail on the base
  commit (RuntimeError / missing helper / loaded.error) and pass here;
  test_load_failure_warning_names_where_it_raised covers the log suffix.

Kanban: t_01a18a72cafa9d67
